{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/801531-ritual-in-changeling","id":801531,"title":"Ritual in Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-05T11:39:53-08:00","id":801531,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Ritual in Changeling","content":"<i>With recent previews about unleashing, I wanted to propose my system for bunks with some examples. Although I named it as Ritual, it is not traditional ritual as when it first comes to the mind. There is no ingredients, but there could be, or candles. Characters just doing their cantrips in a significant way, after some time a pattern occurs. In order to make this process simple, we ritualize that pattern and create some game mechanics for it. You can find my text about ritual and one of my players example for it. I can publish more examples if you guys like it.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Ritual</span><br /> There are many ways of working with glamour, and probably the most common way is called \u201cCantrip\u201d. All cantrips are combinations of specific art, bunk and realm. Thus, this makes them unique, powerful and colorful. However, each of them has different effects, and does not depend on each other.<br /> In time, kithian develops her own way to cast cantrips, and also develops a pattern for bunks. Although, she cannot cast two cantrips at same time as well as cannot cast one cantrip by the help of others, she can use one cantrip to affect another one. However, this process takes reasonable amounts of time.<br /> You can see some example rituals below.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Nightmare</span><br /> Nightmare is a ritual of an Eshu known as \u201cIshtar\u201d. He was a noble Unseelie Elegbra, and known as \u201cKeepers of Nightmares.\u201d He has a treasure called \u201cShername\u201d, which holds nightmares of others.<br /> This ritual is effective at only night, and target must be enchanted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022 Peek through Darkness</span><br /> Peek through Darkness allows caster to perceive the worst nightmare of target. The nightmare appeal as a sentence to caster.<br /> <br /> <b>Bunk:</b> In order to accomplish this, caster must use \u201cDeath\u201d, \u201cDarkness\u201d and \u201cFear\u201d words in one sentence, and target should hear that. Caster cannot use same sentence more than once in her life.<br /> <b>Requirements:</b> 3+ success<b> on \u201c</b>Soothsay 1: Omen\u201d.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022\u2022 Awake the Horrors</span><br /> Awake the Horrors changes the mood of the target. It enforces target to think about her nightmare, and image of the nightmare starts to emerge into target\u2019s mind.<br /> <br /> <b>Bunk:</b> In order to accomplish this, caster should describe and narrate the nightmare. If storytellers like the narration, they can lower the difficulty up to one.<br /> <b>Requirements:</b> 2+ success<b> on \u201c</b>Tale Craft 3: Murmur in the Crowd\u201d.<br /> <b>Bonus:</b> One extra dice for \u201cWhispers of Madness\u201d per success.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022 Whispers of Madness</span><br /> When Whispers of Madness is casted, the fear of the nightmare starts to leak out from target\u2019s mind. It\u2019s voice, smell and aura can be perceived at the surroundings.<br /> <br /> <b>Bunk:</b> In order to achieve this, caster must give a name to nightmare, and whisper it.<br /> <b>Requirements:</b> 3+ success<b> on \u201c</b>Tale Craft 2: Flickering Firelight.\u201d<br /> <b>Bonus:</b> Each three success on this phase gives +1 difficulty to all rolls of target until \u201cUnchain the Terror\u201d is called, and lowers the difficulty for next phase by one.<br /> <b>Special:</b> If 10 success achieved in this phase, storytellers could be think about giving one minor permanent or one major temporary derangement to target.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Unchain the Terror</span><br /> Unchain the Terror calls a chimera which is born from target\u2019s nightmare. It will be hostile to the target. This chimera cannot penetrate the walls or circles that enforced with a light source such as torches or light-bulbs, but not moonlight. Thus, target will be safe in these areas. Also, the chimera shall be extinguished if anyone directly strikes it with a light source.<br /> Caster must give a flaw to the chimera at this phase. For example, for a shadow dragon, it could be weakness to tickling.<br /> <br /> <b>Bunk:</b> In order to achieve this, caster must extinguish at least one light source that was there at the beginning.<br /> <b>Requirements:</b> 3+ success<b> on \u201c</b>Tale Craft 5: Moment of Truth.\u201d<br /> <b>Resistance:</b> Target should roll willpower difficulty equal to casters permanent glamour point at the beginning. Each success subtracts one dice from caster\u2019s base dice pool.<br /> <b>Bonus:</b> Each success gives 5 chimera point. Storyteller should create this chimera. Also, this chimera knows everything about that nightmare, and the target\u2019s thoughts about it.<br /> <b>Treasure:</b> At the end of this phase, the caster can capture the chimera, and bind it to the treasure \u201cShername\u201d. In order to do that, caster should roll willpower, and accomplish at least one success. If she achieves that, spends temporary glamour as many as number of success on Unchain the Terror, and locks the chimera to one page of \u201cShername.\u201d If she fails the check, chimera break free, and can become hostile to caster. Also, all temporary glamour are lost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Step into Unknown</span><br /> Step into Unknown takes target to nearest nightmare realm that suits to target\u2019s fear.<br /> <br /> <b>Bunk:</b> In order to achieve this, caster must push the target into darkness. If target knows the place well, storytellers can raise the difficulty.<br /> <b>Requirements:</b> 3+ success<b> on \u201c</b>Wayfare 3: Portal Passage\u201d. \u201cFae 3: Manifold Chimera\u201d is compulsory.<br /> <b>Reference:</b> Rules of \u201cOpen a Rath\u201d are valid.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Taste the Fear</span><br /> Rather than a phase of the ritual, Taste the Fear is a life saver that helps the caster. If caster cannot find anything to narrate about the nightmare they can just peek the mind of the target, and take some details about it. Taste the Fear can only be used before Awake the Horrors and Whispers of Madness.<br /> <br /> <b>Bunk:</b> In order to achieve this, caster must look at the eyes of target, and continue her narration.<br /> <b>Bonus:</b> Each success on \u201cTale Craft 1: Agemo\u2019s Blessing\u201d gives one word about the nightmare. Storytellers who like the given details in the narration of the caster, can lower the difficulty by one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Treasures</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Shername</span><br /> Shername, also known as Book of Nightmares, is a treasure that keeps the nightmares of others. The very first page of the Shername keeps the nightmare of the bearer, and legends claim that nobody dared to open that page. The last master of the Shername is an unseelie Eshu known as \u201cIshtar.\u201d<br /> Sher means trouble, and when you see Sher, you know that trouble is on the way.<br /> <br /> <b>Transformation:</b> Shername can change form at nights. It can change into \u201cGrim Reaper\u201d like form called Sher. Sher could talk, but generally not chose to do so. Shername can also transform into one of the recorded nightmares with cost of one glamour point. However it cannot be used more than once at same night.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T02:28:58-08:00","id":801894,"title":"","content":"These are interesting as examples of alternate ways to combine Bunks, Arts and Realms in specific ways that changelings can tailor. Kinda like combi Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T10:02:21-08:00","id":802188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/801531-ritual-in-changeling?p=801894#post801894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are interesting as examples of alternate ways to combine Bunks, Arts and Realms in specific ways that changelings can tailor. Kinda like combi Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Yea, actually my purpose behind this was that. I will publish one more example called as &quot;Mirage&quot;. Same eshu did that to use it at Day time.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}